                         "markdown":  "### OT Cyber Document Tool\n- A new tool for documents that are not assessment or risk reports but should look like one: proposals, method statements, reports, procedures and short notes.\n- A document with a cover prints with the same cover, document control page, header and footer as an assessment report. A short document has no cover and opens with its title.\n- Write in an editor with headings, paragraphs, bulleted and numbered lists, tables, pictures, footnotes, links, page breaks and landscape pages. The template decides fonts, sizes and colours, so every document looks the same.\n- Red prompts mark what is still to write. The Issue check lists them, and a Final export is refused while any remain.\n- Export a Word file as a Draft, with a watermark, or as a Final, which opens read-only.\n- Optional numbered headings and a Contents list of linked headings.\n- The cover is always one page, and the footer carries the document\u0027s own classification.\n- A picture taller than a page, such as a phone screenshot, is fitted to the page.\n- Pasting from Word carries footnotes, and says what it left out: comments, tracked deletions, pictures it could not read.\n\n### Bringing in a Word file\n- Load a `.docx` and it is rebuilt in the SolutionsPT template: headings, lists, tables, footnotes and links become the template\u0027s own.\n- Pictures are kept. Charts, SmartArt, shapes, text boxes, embedded sheets and equations are carried across as they were and print in the Word export, made smaller only where one would not fit the page.\n- A drawing that floated beside the text stays beside the same words, and a diagram drawn as loose shapes and lines is kept whole.\n- Anything that could not be carried over, such as comments, headers and footers, hidden text or a hand-made cover, is listed after the import, with a link to where it was. So is anything that was changed, such as list and heading numbers that no longer match a reference in the text.\n- A Word report from the assessment or risk tool, or a document exported by the document tool, has its SolutionsPT cover and document control page recognised: they are taken out, Document information is filled from them, and the export prints the current template\u0027s pages. One button on the import report puts the originals back, and another takes them out again.\n- A first page that looks like another company\u0027s cover is pointed out on the import report, with a button to remove it.\n- The Word file you load is never changed.\n- Charts drawn as tables keep their look: a report\u0027s tiles, stacked bars, heatmaps and coloured cells come across with their fills, widths and borders, legend squares keep their colours, and they print in the Word export as they were. An ordinary table still takes the template\u0027s look.\n\n### Word preview in the assessment and risk tools\n- A new Word preview page, beside the report page, shows the Word report as Export Word makes it, page by page: the cover, document control, then the body, with landscape pages, charts and coloured tables as they print. It is drawn from the Word file itself, so it cannot disagree with it.\n- In the assessment tool it follows the export\u0027s choices: Draft or Final, which site, zone or product, or the organisation-wide report. In the risk tool it shows the detailed or the high-level report.\n- The report is still written and edited on the report page; the preview builds again when anything changes.\n\n### Saving and files\n- The document tool saves its own document file, in place where the browser allows, with an autosave copy and a warning before unsaved changes are lost.\n- A document file and a Word file both open with Load in the document tool.\n- Save as makes a separate document, with its own autosave copy. Two windows of the tool can be open without one disturbing the other\u0027s unsaved work.\n\n### SolutionsPT OT Cyber Suite\n- The home page has a fourth card and the rail a fourth button, Write, for the document tool, with a tour of a demo proposal.\n- A document file dropped anywhere in the suite, or chosen with Open a file, opens in the document tool. A Word file is opened with Load in the document tool itself, and so is a document file over 100 MB.\n- The document tool works on its own: no file passes between it and the other tools.\n\n### OT Cyber Report Review Tool\n- The report a reviewer reads and comments on is shown as A4 pages, opening on the house cover with the client, site, title, issue, author and classification. Word decides where the pages break. The lines on the cover can be commented on like any other text. Commenting, suggestions, the checklist, the automatic checks and the keyboard work as before.\n\nSaved project files from v0.5, v0.5.1 and v0.6 open unchanged."
